# AppBrain

> AppBrain has data on 2M+ Google Play apps with 10+ years of history: keyword rankings, download estimates, competitors, app metadata, and the SDKs each app uses. Developers use it to track keywords, research competitors, and promote or monetize Android apps.

AI agents can query AppBrain directly through its remote MCP server at `https://api.appbrain.com/mcp` (streamable HTTP, OAuth 2.1, no API key). To set it up for a user, fetch the setup instructions below and follow them.

## Connect an AI agent

- [MCP setup instructions for agents](https://www.appbrain.com/docs/api/mcp-setup.md): Step-by-step for an agent connecting itself: adding the server, the sign-in screen, checking the connection, credit costs
- [MCP server documentation](https://www.appbrain.com/docs/api/mcp): What the MCP server can do, for the user
- [AppBrain CLI](https://www.appbrain.com/docs/api/cli): Command-line client for the Keyword API with JSON output, for agents without MCP support

## API

- [Using the AppBrain API](https://www.appbrain.com/docs/api/appbrain-api): Overview of the REST API for app data and promotion campaigns
